# Vercel: selected automatically when VERCEL=1.
# To exercise cloud integrations from local development, set:
# CONVERSION_BACKEND=vercel
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://... (Neon integration, server-side only)
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=... (PRIVATE Vercel Blob store; client-upload token issuance)
# CONVERSION_SANDBOX_IMAGE=auden-conversion:v1
# CRON_SECRET=... (random secret for the cleanup fallback, at least 32 characters)
# Vercel Sandbox uses deployment OIDC automatically; never expose credentials
# as NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables. For local cloud testing, use `vercel env pull`.
# Optional local/CI Sandbox fallback when OIDC isn't available:
# VERCEL_TOKEN=...
# VERCEL_TEAM_ID=...
# VERCEL_PROJECT_ID=...
# APP_ORIGIN=https://tools.example.com
# Leave APP_ORIGIN unset in Preview so its own origin is accepted.

# Local development: Next.js and the worker share the same absolute directory.
# The default is .data/conversions relative to apps/web.
# CONVERSION_DATA_DIR=/absolute/path/to/conversions
# APP_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
# FFMPEG_PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin/ffmpeg
# FFPROBE_PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin/ffprobe
# LIBREOFFICE_PATH=/Applications/LibreOffice.app/Contents/MacOS/soffice
